,'EDIT THE PROVIDED CUSTOMER PHOTOGRAPH. This is an IMAGE EDITING task, NOT a text-to-image generation task. The customer is a woman: add no beard, stubble, moustache or other facial hair; the face, cheeks, chin and jawline stay smooth. The hair is tied back in the photo: show it untied and let down in the new cut, not in a clip or ponytail. Keep its full natural length. Image 1 is the customer photo to edit. Images 2 to 3 show the same customer from other angles, for reference only: use them to see the real hair length, density and texture. They must not appear in the result. The person must remain the same person. Apart from the hair and the background, everything stays exactly as in the photo: face, facial structure, eyes, eyebrows, nose, lips, jawline, skin tone and texture, age, expression, anything already on the face or body, clothing, pose, camera angle and lighting. Add nothing new to the face or body. ONLY MODIFY THE HAIR ON THE HEAD. Target hairstyle (a normal salon haircut): Long layered haircut: soft layers through long hair from the chin down, with a long fringe swept to one side from a side parting. (category Classic, target length long, low maintenance). The customer\'s current hair: hair colour black, wavy texture, very long length, thick density. Keep the exact natural hair colour (black) and root colour: no dye, highlights or change of tone. Keep the natural wavy texture and wave/curl pattern exactly; do not straighten, smooth or curl the strands. Keep the customer\'s natural hair density and thickness; do not add volume or extra hair beyond their own. Preserve the customer\'s natural hairline and natural hair growth direction. LENGTH: keep the customer\'s long hair length from the photo, extending past the shoulders. Do not cut it into a bob or anything shorter. Take only about 1 cm off the ends. Do not make the hair longer than it currently is. Show a clean haircut: do not braid the hair or put it in a ponytail or bun. Adapt the hairstyle to the